===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷṓws|*tewh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|buter}}, {{m|enm|butter}}, from {{inh|en|ang|butere}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*buterā}}, from {{der|en|la|būtȳrum}}, from {{der|en|grc|βούτῡρον||cow cheese}}, compound of {{m|grc|βοῦς||ox, cow}} and {{m|grc|τῡρός||cheese}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A soft, fatty foodstuff made by [[churn]]ing the [[cream]] of [[milk]] (generally cow's milk).
# Any of various foodstuffs made from other foods or oils, similar in consistency to, eaten like or intended as a substitute for butter (''preceded by the name of the food used to make it'').
#: {{ux|en|peanut '''butter'''}}
#: {{ux|en|soy '''butter'''}}
#: {{ux|en|chocolate '''butter'''}}
# Any of various substances made from other (especially plant-based) oils or fats, used in [[moisturizer]]s, [[cosmetics]], etc.
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2016-09-07|author=Elaine Stavert|title=Beauty Oils & Butter|publisher=GMC PUBLICATIONS LTD|isbn=9781861087126
|text='''Butters''' such as cocoa, illippe, kokum, mango, murumuru, sal (shorea) and shea occur naturally and are obtained directly from the plant.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2019-04-05|author=Heather A.E. Benson; Michael S. Roberts; Vania Rodrigues Leite-Silva; Kenneth Walters|title=Cosmetic Formulation: Principles and Practice|publisher=CRC Press|isbn=9781482235401|page=227
|text='''Butters''' are triglycerides {{...|that generally have a titer point between 20°C and 40.5°C, at which the mixture of fatty acids solidifies}}. ''Cocoa '''butter''''' (''Theobroma cacao'') is used as an emollient in topical cosmetic formulations, {{...}} South American and the Brazilian rainforest offer various plants with common '''butters''' used in the industry that include {{...}} cupuaçu '''butter''' {{...}} and murumuru butter from the murumuru palm tree (''Astrocaryum murumuru''). India is another source of many '''butters''' used in cosmetic products, including kokum '''butter''' extracted from the seeds of the ''Garcinia indica'' tree, mango '''butter''' from the ''Mangifera indica'' tree and shea '''butter'''{{nb...}}}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|chemistry}} Any specific [[soft]] [[substance]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Butter''' of antimony; '''butter''' of arsenic}}
# {{lb|en|aviation|slang}} A smooth plane landing.
#: ''That landing was total '''butter'''!''

